=== expr follows GNU expr's grammar
4.2MP : [^0-9]*[0-9]*.\([0-9]*\) => [2] 0
abc : a\(b\) => [b] 0
abc : ab => [2] 0
abc : x\(y\) => [] 1
1 + 2 => [3] 0
2 * 3 + 1 => [7] 0
7 / 0 => [] 2
a + 1 => [] 2
0 |  => [0] 1
 | 5 => [5] 0
3 & 0 => [0] 1
3 & 4 => [3] 0
a < b => [1] 0
10 < 9 => [0] 1
10 < 9a => [1] 0
length abcd => [4] 0
substr hello 2 3 => [ell] 0
index hello lo => [3] 0
match abc a\(.\) => [b] 0
( 1 + 2 ) * 3 => [9] 0
( 1 + 2 => [] 2
1 + => [] 2
1 2 => [] 2
+ length => [length] 0
length => [] 2
00 => [00] 1
-0 => [-0] 1
 => [] 2
-- 5 => [5] 0
